    "created_at": "2023-10-04T03:52:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-04T03:52:34Z",
    "body": "> Would it make sense to make this change as part of \"update document for history step application\"?\r\n\r\nNot really, because most types of history step application do not change the URL of the document. Any cross-document navigation/traversal either creates a new document from scratch, or reuses an existing document from bfcache (with no URL change). It's only same-document navigations that need to change the document's URL, and only one of those uses \"update document for history step application\", per the note in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-non-frag-sync:update-document-for-history-step-application .",
